    "node_id": "I_kwDORdC75M8AAAABMGF3zQ",
    "title": "[bug] Remapping keeps deleted and renamed symbols in the graph",
    "body": "## Description\n\nAfter a successful incremental `ix map`, symbols removed by a rename or file deletion remain queryable in the graph. A deleted file can report a clean workspace even though its old nodes and incident edges are still present.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n1. Create a small TypeScript project with `src/provider.ts` exporting `removedTarget` and `src/caller.ts` importing and calling it.\n2. Run `ix map . --silent` and confirm `ix callers removedTarget --format json` returns the caller.\n3. Either rename `removedTarget` in both files or delete `src/provider.ts`.\n4. Run `ix map . --silent` again.\n5. Run `ix locate removedTarget --format json`.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nEntities no longer emitted by the current source should be removed with their incident edges. If a deleted provider file is later recreated, surviving callers should be re-ingested so their dependency edges are restored.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe old symbol remains resolvable after a rename, so repeated renames accumulate stale graph entities. Deleting the provider also leaves its old symbol and caller edge behind even though the map finishes successfully.\n\n## CLI output\n\nAfter deleting the provider and remapping with Ix 0.9.1:\n\n```text\n$ ix map . --silent\nmap: 3 files ...\n\n$ ix locate removedTarget --format json\n\"resolvedTarget\": { \"kind\": \"function\", \"name\": \"removedTarget\", \"path\": \"src/provider.ts\" }\n```\n\n## Environment\n- OS: macOS 26.6.1\n- Node: 26.7.0\n- Ix version: 0.9.1\n",
    "state": "closed",
    "state_reason": "completed",
